{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "גור אריה יהודה", :translit "gur aryeh yehudah", :gloss "a lion's whelp is Judah"} {:he "דוד", :translit "david", :gloss "David"} {:he "שלמה", :translit "shlomo", :gloss "Solomon"} {:he "נחשון", :translit "nachshon", :gloss "Nahshon"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "גור אריה יהודה", :b "דוד"} {:kind :gematria, :a "גור אריה יהודה", :b "שלמה"} {:kind :gematria, :a "גור אריה יהודה", :b "נחשון"}], :frame {:text "Jacob's blessing to Judah, 'a lion's whelp is Judah' (Genesis 49:9), is read as encoding the names of David, Solomon, and Nahshon, who are all descendants of the tribe of Judah. David was established as king over Israel (2 Samuel 5:3), Solomon his son reigned after him (1 Kings 2:12), and Nahshon son of Amminadab was the tribal prince of Judah (Numbers 1:7) identified in rabbinic tradition as the first to enter the Sea of Reeds (Sotah 37a).", :sources ["Genesis 49:9" "Numbers 1:7" "2 Samuel 5:3" "1 Kings 2:12" "Sotah 37a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "גור אריה יהודה", :translit "gur aryeh yehudah", :gloss "a lion's whelp is Judah"} {:he "דוד", :translit "david", :gloss "David"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "גור אריה יהודה", :spells "דוד"}], :frame nil} {:quotes [{:he "עלית", :translit "alit", :gloss "you went up"} {:he "מטרף בני עלית", :translit "mi-teref beni alit", :gloss "from the prey my son you went up"} {:he "כי עלית משכבי אביך", :translit "ki alit mishkavi avicha", :gloss "for you went up my father's bed"} {:he "עלית למרום", :translit "alit l'marom", :gloss "you went up on high"} {:he "ויתן עוז למלכו", :translit "v'yiten oz l'malcho", :gloss "and He gave strength to His king"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["מטרף בני עלית" "כי עלית משכבי אביך" "עלית למרום"]}], :frame {:text "Reuben lost the birthright because he defiled his father's bed, as stated at Genesis 49:4, 'for you went up (כי עלית) my father's bed'; 1 Chronicles 5:1–2 records that the birthright was transferred to Joseph and the leadership (נחלה) to Judah. Kingship and priesthood are described as divine gifts; Psalm 2:6 says 'I have set My king on Zion,' and 1 Samuel 2:28 refers to the priesthood as a grant (נתתי). The verse 'He gives strength to His king' (1 Samuel 2:10) and 'He gives great salvations to His king' (2 Samuel 22:51) frame kingship as a divine bestowal. Jacob's blessing to Judah in Genesis 49:8–10 confers the scepter and ruler's staff.", :sources ["Genesis 49:4" "Genesis 49:8–10" "1 Chronicles 5:1-2" "1 Samuel 2:10" "2 Samuel 22:51"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "גור אריה יהודה", :a-value 455, :b "דוד", :b-value 14, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "גור אריה יהודה", :a-value 455, :b "שלמה", :b-value 375, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "גור אריה יהודה", :a-value 455, :b "נחשון", :b-value 414, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "גור אריה יהודה", :spells "דוד", :letters ["ג" "א" "י"], :by :selah, :order :mismatch} {:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["מטרף בני עלית" "כי עלית משכבי אביך" "עלית למרום"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "מטרף בני עלית", :refs ["Genesis 49:9"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "כי עלית משכבי אביך", :refs ["Genesis 49:4"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "עלית למרום", :refs ["Psalms 68:19"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:12:26.870585440Z", :model "glm-5.2"}